# File: tests/features/add_greeting_url_encoded_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/217-add-greeting-url-encoded-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Percent-encode the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Return the percent-encoded greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_url_encoded is called with Ada
    Then the result is the Python str Hello%2C%20Ada

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Encode reserved characters and UTF-8 bytes, keep unreserved characters
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_url_encoded is called with A/B&C~d_e.f and with Zo followed by precomposed U+00EB
    Then the results are Hello%2C%20A%2FB%26C~d_e.f and Hello%2C%20Zo%C3%AB
    And every result character is an unreserved character or a percent sign

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Decoding restores the greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When urllib.parse.unquote is applied to greeting_url_encoded of Ada, Zo followed by U+00EB, and A/B&C~d_e.f
    Then each result equals greet of the same name

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_url_encoded is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing existing surfaces
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_url_encoded of Ada, and nmg-smoke Ada runs
    Then the example prints Hello%2C%20Ada
    And greeting_url_encoded is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__ alongside every previously listed export
    And nmg-smoke prints Hello, Ada with one newline and exit status 0
    And the README documents UTF-8 percent-encoding of the complete greeting, the unreserved set, and the inherited invalid-name error
